    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαντλ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw off from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. χθονὸς ὕβρισμα θνητῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1641
				</span></i>
			; <i>lighten,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί σοι οἷοί τε θνητοὶ τῶνδ᾽
					ἀπαντλῆσαι πόνων;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸ ὑγρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					870b16
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιχέω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				407d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.
			only, <i>lighten, lessen,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάρος ψυχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					354
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐγκαλουμένων ἀπηντληκώς τι</span>
			<i>having shed</i> some of his faults, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.35
			</span></i> O.:—in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.266
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				57
			</span></i>.</div>
